# NexCV — Cursor Rules

Read `.ai/instructions.md` completely before making any changes. It is the single source of truth for this project.

Also read:
- `rules.md` — mandatory coding, architecture, and git standards
- `skills.md` — architecture patterns and project roadmap

## Architecture at a glance

This is a monorepo with three sub-projects:
- `nexcv-application/` — Flutter app (Clean Architecture, Riverpod, GoRouter)
- `nexcv-backend/` — Spring Boot 3 / Java 21 / Maven
- `nexcv-portal/` — Angular 17+ standalone components

## Always-on rules

### Flutter
- Feature structure: `domain/` → `data/` → `presentation/`. Dependencies inward only.
- Riverpod: `riverpod_annotation` code gen only. Run `flutter pub run build_runner build` after adding providers.
- Routing: GoRouter only. Never `Navigator.push`.
- Models: Freezed + JsonSerializable. Never hand-write `fromJson`/`toJson`.
- HTTP: Dio through `RemoteDataSource` only. Never call Dio from a provider or widget.
- Tokens: `flutter_secure_storage`. Never SharedPreferences.

### UI / Stitch designs
- Reference: `stitch_nexcv_ats_builder/{screen}/screen.png` is the pixel-perfect target.
- `code.html` files show layout hierarchy and spacing — use for reference, never copy HTML into Dart.
- Shared widgets go in `lib/shared/widgets/`. No duplicate widget code across features.
- Design tokens (colors, spacing, typography, radii) are defined in `.ai/instructions.md` — use them, don't invent new values.

### Spring Boot
- Build tool: **Maven** (`./mvnw`). Never Gradle.
- Every schema change = Flyway migration. Never modify existing migration files.
- All responses: `ApiResponse<T>`. All exceptions: `GlobalExceptionHandler`.
- Transaction boundary: service layer only. No `@Transactional` on controllers.

### Angular
- Standalone components only. No NgModules for features.
- `OnPush` change detection on all presentational components.
- HTTP: `ApiService` only. Never `HttpClient` in components.
- Subscriptions: `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `async` pipe.

### Git
- Branch: `feature/NCV-{id}-{slug}` targeting `develop`.
- Commits: `feat(scope): description` (Conventional Commits, ≤72 chars).
